      ],
      "documentation": [
        "https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine",
        "https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine/releases/tag/v1.18.0",
        "https://packages.ubuntu.com/noble/hyperfine"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "command": "/usr/bin/hyperfine --warmup 3 --runs 10 --export-json timings.json './program-a' './program-b'",
          "description": "Compare two executable commands and retain individual timing samples."
        },
        {
          "command": "/usr/bin/hyperfine --shell=none --runs 10 --export-json timings.json './program'",
          "description": "Measure a direct executable without a shell wrapper."
        }
      ],
      "locations": [
        {
          "label": "Hyperfine",
          "path": "/usr/bin/hyperfine",
          "purpose": "APT-managed command timing executable."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The functional check confirms one warmup plus three measured child executions, validates JSON raw samples and summary statistics, and verifies that a nonzero-exit child fails the run.",
        "Choose warm/cold-cache conditions, CPU affinity and workload controls in experiment code. This tool does not replace any official Benchmark timer, validation or aggregation protocol.",
        "Do not silently enable --ignore-failure in a qualification run. Invalid command executions are not successful timing results.",
        "This explicit revision removes only an accidentally archived Python bytecode cache. The original authored check and exact APT source locks are unchanged. No installation, compilation or functional check was executed."
      ],
      "summary": "Run repeated command timing experiments with warmups and raw JSON samples; compare compiler builds or programs while preserving measurement failures."
